      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "SOLID GROOVE (8) pinged the lids from the inside draw and led until late, finishing third and beaten 0.7 lengths (25.72) at Shepparton in a Grade 5 over 450m. Racing well and deserves a win. MAD HATTER ROSE (3) was strongly fancied last time and hit the ground running with a slick early split, giving a sight but could manage only second (24.54) at this track over 435m. The form out of her last race has been franked. Hard to beat again. BE MY TIGER (2) continues to build a strong record, last start jumping favourite and hit the ground running, leading throughout to score (20.14) at Traralgon in T3 Grade 6 over 350m. Fast beginner who should quickly stride to the lead. The form from her last run stacks up well. Looks a key chance if runs up to latest figure. ",
